# openyaga -- deny by default.
#
# The repo lives in its own folder, beside the game, the disc image and
# everything extracted from them:
#
#     <workspace>/openyaga/          this repo
#     <workspace>/stock-game-files/  the installed game
#     <workspace>/extracted/ ...     tools output
#
# Even so, nothing is tracked unless it is listed below, so an accidental
# `git add -A` adds nothing new.  The flip side: a new top-level file is
# ignored until it is listed here -- LICENSE and XML.md went unpublished for
# exactly that reason.

/*

!.gitignore
!README.md
!FORMATS.md
!XML.md
!ENGINE_API.md
!LICENSE
!tools/
!player/
# One illustrative screenshot for the README.
!docs/

# Reconstructed game source: a derivative work of the original program.
# It belongs only on a machine that owns the game.  Never commit it.
player/gamecache/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
